# Line endings ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Git's system config on this machine sets core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# text files to CRLF on checkout while the committed blobs stay LF. Anything
# that hashes the WORKING TREE -- provenance stamps, frozen-evidence pins,
# parity manifests, engine identities -- then records a digest that depends on
# which machine or git config did the checkout, not on the content.
#
# This has bitten the trading stack repeatedly: strategy-analysis on
# 2026-09-09 (a checkout rewrote six frozen files LF->CRLF; git showed them
# clean while every pin failed), and trading-capability-hub on 2026-09-20
# (manifest drift across a branch merge, and engine identities that changed
# with no code change). See the hub's
# docs/audits/NT_ANALYZER_RUN_REFUSAL_ROOT_CAUSE_2026-09-20.md and commit
# "Make engine identity independent of line endings".
#
# Pin the working tree to LF everywhere. Any path rule FURTHER DOWN this file
# overrides this default -- keep byte-exact rules (-text) below it, never above.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows formats that genuinely require CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.sln text eol=crlf

# Binary payloads must never be line-ending converted. text=auto already
# detects most of these; listing them makes the intent explicit.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.7z binary
*.gz binary
*.parquet binary
*.feather binary
*.pkl binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pyd binary
*.so binary
